of
315
English
local
authorities
between
September
2020
and
June
2021
.
This
analysis
reveals
a
series
of
subepidemics
that
peaked
in
early
autumn
2020
,
followed
by
a
jump
in
transmissibility
of
the
B
.
1
.
1
.
7
/
Alpha
lineage
.
The
Alpha
variant
grew
when
other
lineages
declined
during
the
second
national
lockdown
and
regionally
tiered
restrictions
between
November
and
December
2020
.
A
third
more
stringent
national
lockdown
suppressed
the
Alpha
variant
and
eliminated
