of
hospitalized
adolescents
to
illustrate
the
application
of
trauma-informed
principles
of
care
with
this
unique
population
.
Recent
Findings
Adolescents
today
are
caught
in
the
crosshairs
of
two
syndemics
:
racism
and
other
structural
inequities
and
the
COVID-19
pandemic
.
Increased
hospitalizations
and
mental
health
diagnoses
during
the
past
two
years
signal
toxic
levels
of
stress
affecting
this
group
.
Trauma-informed
care
promotes
health
,
healing
,
and
equity
.
Summary
This
concept
of
the
"
trauma-informed
approach
"
is
still
novel
;
through
examples
and
practice
,
providers
can
learn
to
universally
apply
the
trauma-informed
care
framework
to
every
patient
encounter
to
address
the
harmful
effects
of
trauma
and
promote
recovery
and
resilience
.
.
