portrays
a
general
increase
from
the
onset
of
the
pandemic
in
the
country
to
about
day
160
after
which
there
is
a
general
decrease
onward
.
We
fitted
a
zero-inflated
Poisson
autoregressive
model
and
zero-inflated
negative
binomial
autoregressive
model
to
the
data
in
the
partial-likelihood
framework
.
The
zero-inflated
negative
binomial
autoregressive
model
outperformed
