.
N95
mask
shortages
were
associated
with
increased
odds
of
at
least
1
COVID-19
case
[
odds
ratio
(
OR
)
1
.
21
,
95
%
confidence
interval
(
CI
)
1
.
05-1
.
40
]
and
hospitalization
(
1
.
26
,
95
%
CI
1
.
13-1
.
40
)
,
