###PMID=33989322
Closed
for
business
:
The
mortality
impact
of
business
closures
during
the
Covid-19
pandemic
We
investigate
the
effectiveness
of
business
shutdowns
to
contain
the
Covid-19
disease
.
In
March
2020
,
Italy
shut
down
operations
in
selected
sectors
of
its
economy
.
Using
a
difference-in-differences
approach
,
we
find
that
municipalities
with
higher
exposure
to
closed
sectors
experienced
subsequently
lower
mortality
rates
.
The
implied
life
savings
exceed
9
,
400
people
over
a
period
of
less
than
a
month
.
We
also
find
that
business
closures
exhibited
rapidly
diminishing
returns
and
had
large
effects
outside
the
closed
businesses
themselves
,
including
spillovers
to
other
municipalities
.
Overall
,
the
results
suggest
business
shutdowns
are
effective
,
but
should
be
selectively
implemented
and
centrally
coordinated
.
.
