and
range
of
use
.
Here
,
we
present
Exerscent
,
a
portable
,
low-cost
olfactory
display
designed
primarily
for
uses
outside
of
the
laboratory
and
that
can
be
operated
with
a
personal
computer
.
Exerscent
includes
Radio
Frequency
Identification
(
RFID
)
tags
that
are
attached
to
odor
stimuli
and
read
with
a
MFRC522
module
RFID
reader
/
antenna
that
encodes
the
odor
in
order
to
provide
adaptive
challenges
for
the
user
(
e
.
g
.
,
an
odor
identification
task
)
.
Hardware
parts
are
commercially
available
or
3D
printed
.
Instructions
and
code
for
building
the
Exerscent
are
freely
available
online
(
https
:
/
/
osf
.
io
/
kwftm
/
)
.
As
a
proof
of
