samples
.
Even
the
SARS-CoV-2
virus
titers
were
undetectable
in
feces
,
it
could
be
positive
again
soon
and
likely
related
to
fluctuated
inflammation
levels
(
interleukin-6
,
etc
.
)
and
lowered
immune
responses
(
CD4
+
T
lymphocyte
,
etc
.
)
.
Our
findings
expand
the
novel
understanding
of
the
breadth
of
concomitant
virological
features
during
a
non-severe
